 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "dirs and files are disjoint lists of absolute paths; edges are [parent, child] pairs where parent is a directory and child = parent + \"/\" + name. Every file and every non-root directory has exactly one parent edge. getAllFiles(dir) lists a directory's children in the order their edges appear, and delete(p) only removes a file or an empty directory. Delete path and everything below it using only those operations: children first, in getAllFiles order, each subtree completely, then the directory itself. Return the paths in the order delete is called; return [] when path does not exist.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk06-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
